`base64` encodes or decodes data in Base64 format. Base64 is a way of representing binary or text data using only 64 printable ASCII characters (A-Z, a-z, 0-9, +, /). It is commonly used to encode data for transmission over text-based protocols like email or HTTP, and is easily recognisable by its alphanumeric characters and `=` or `==` padding at the end.

