| `-i` | Ignore non-alphabet characters when decoding |
| `-w <number>` | Wrap encoded output at specified column e.g. `-w 0` disables line wrapping |

Base64 is NOT encryption — it is just an encoding scheme. Anyone can decode it instantly. Never confuse encoding with security.


**Level 11 - Level 12: The password for the next level is stored in the file data.txt, where all lowercase (a-z) and uppercase (A-Z) letters have been rotated by 13 positions

    ssh bandit11@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220
    password: dtR173fZKb0RRsDFSGsg2RWnpNVj3qRr

